    "title": "This Minnesota Train Turns A 3-Hour Ride Into A Fine Dining Journey Through The Countryside - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Micah Dawson ,\n1 days ago Three hours on a train doesn’t usually come with white tablecloths and a full dining service. Here, it does, scenery included as a bonus nobody complains about. Courses arrive timed to the ride itself, plates changing roughly as often as the view does outside the window. Forests give way to lakeshore, lakeshore gives way to small towns, and somewhere between courses two and three, most passengers stop checking their phones entirely. Read full article\n23",
